      "text": "First, we need to evaluate the given operation \\((a \\Diamond b) = ab^2 - b + 1\\) with \\(a = -1\\) and \\(b = 6\\). We will substitute these values into the operation to find the result.\n\nThe expression becomes:\n\\[\n(-1) \\Diamond 6 = (-1) \\cdot 6^2 - 6 + 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(6^2\\):\n\\[\n6^2 = 36\n\\]\n\nNow substitute \\(36\\) back into the expression:\n\\[\n(-1) \\cdot 36 - 6 + 1\n\\]\n\nPerform the multiplication:\n\\[\n-1 \\cdot 36 = -36\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(-36\\) into the expression:\n\\[\n-36 - 6 + 1\n\\]\n\nNow, perform the subtraction and addition from left to right:\n\\[\n-36 - 6 = -42\n\\]\n\\[\n-42 + 1 = -41\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\((-1) \\Diamond 6\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-41}\n\\]",
